  "summary": "Distinctive embroidery style from Poland's Podhale region featuring curved, horn-like patterns on clothing.",
  "description": "Parzenica embroidery consists of intricate curved, horn-shaped designs typically executed in red thread on white or blue fabric, forming symmetrical patterns across the chest area of traditional garments. This technique developed among the Goral (highland) people of the Tatra Mountains region, with the parzenica motif possibly symbolizing protection and fertility, while the geometric precision reflects the mountain community's cultural identity and connection to nature.",
